> Do you think the codes snytax are correct in terms of analyzing the relationship between the two separate processes?

Why are you freeing the latent scales after the first occasion?  Is that model even identified?  Fixing the thresholds only allows the growth in the latent means to be identified.  You would need 3+ categories (2+ thresholds) to additionally identify variance of the latent item responses.

> How do I interpret the covariance between the two intercepts - I mean, are the estimates for dichotomous variable comparable to those produced for continuous variable?

You are modeling growth in a binary variable using a probit link, so the interpretation is about the latent normal variable that is assumed to underlie the observed dichotomous variable. You should probably read this:

Mehta, P. D., Neale, M. C., & Flay, B. R. (2004). Squeezing interval change from ordinal panel data: Latent growth curves with ordinal outcomes. Psychological Methods, 9(3), 301–333. https://doi.org/10.1037/1082-989X.9.3.301 <https://psycnet.apa.org/doi/10.1037/1082-989X.9.3.301>

