> 1. When I examine this without any control variable, I get a significant negative slope (-.132***) with significant variance, indicating that job demands decrease over time.
> But, when I add control variables including age at T1(time-invariant), and job characteristics (time-variant), I get positive slope (.338***) with insignificant variance.

This is regression.  Without a predictor, the intercept of an "outcome" is the grand mean.  When you add a predictor, the intercept is the expected value when the predictor(s) == 0.  If you mean-center your predictor(s), you will get the same intercepts as in the model without predictors.  That's not a recommendation, just to get you started thinking about how your model works.

