My understanding is that if my measurement model meets for strict invariance, I should constrain the residual variances (and covariances?) of the observed variables so that the variance and covariance is fully captured by the latent growth factors. However, all the above factors load onto the same superordinate highly, and are highly correlated with one another. I'm assuming that much of my poor model fit is because of this. I'd very much appreciate any guidance you can provide.

