I would include the green paths as well, otherwise your indirect effects are hard to interpret.  If you only estimate the yellow paths, then the "b" (and "c") paths are interpreted as controlling for the confounders, but the "a" paths would not.  Seems strange to calculate indirect effects from mismatched direct effects.

